{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1750","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Bracket Cost"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Daemon Targaryen decided to stop looking like a Metin2 character. He turned himself into the most beautiful thing, a bracket sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a bracket sequence, we can do two kind of operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select one of its substrings$$$^\\dagger$$$ and cyclic shift it to the right. For example, after a cyclic shift to the right, \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will become \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Insert any bracket, opening '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' or closing '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', wherever you want in the sequence. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We define the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cost"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a bracket sequence as the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number of such operations to make it balanced$$$^\\ddagger$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given a bracket sequence $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, find the sum of costs across all its $$$\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$$$ non-empty substrings. Note that for each substring we calculate the cost "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"independently"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\dagger$$$ A string $$$a$$$ is a substring of a string $$$b$$$ if $$$a$$$ can be obtained from $$$b$$$ by deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) characters from the beginning and several (possibly, zero or all) characters from the end."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\ddagger$$$ A sequence of brackets is called balanced if one can turn it into a valid math expression by adding characters $$$+$$$ and $$$1$$$. For example, sequences \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()(()))"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are balanced, while \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()))("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10^5$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the bracket sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains a string $$$s$$$, consisting only of characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', of length $$$n$$$ — the bracket sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that sum of $$$n$$$ across all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single integer — the sum of costs of all substrings of $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1\n)\n4\n)()(\n3\n())\n5\n(((((\n10\n)(())))())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n9\n6\n35\n112\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, there is the only substring \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Its cost is $$$1$$$ because we can insert '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' to the beginning of this substring and get a string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", that is a balanced string."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the cost of each substring of length one is $$$1$$$. The cost of a substring \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is $$$1$$$ because we can cyclically shift it to right and get a string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". The cost of strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is $$$1$$$ because its enough to insert one bracket to each of them. The cost of substring \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")()("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is $$$1$$$ because we can cyclically shift it to right and get a string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". So there are $$$4 + 2 + 2 + 1 = 9$$$ substring of cost $$$1$$$ and $$$1$$$ substring of cost $$$0$$$. So the sum of the costs is $$$9$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the cost is $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the cost is $$$0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the cost is $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the cost is $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"))"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the cost is $$$2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the cost is $$$1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So the sum of the costs is $$$6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1750E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1750/problem/E"}